  "title": "Erdős Problem #1117",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f(z)$ be an entire function which is not a monomial. Let $\nu(r)$ count the number of $z$ with $\\lvert z\\rvert=r$ such that $\\lvert f(z)\\rvert=\\max_{\\lvert z\\rvert=r}\\lvert f(z)\\rvert$. (This is a finite quantity if $f$ is not a monomial.)\nIs it possible for $ \\limsup \nu(r)=\\infty? $ Is it possible for $ \\liminf \nu(r)=\\infty? $ ",
